## 8. Automatic Database Update Architecture

The reference application advertises automatic database updates without requiring a new application release.

This is a major product requirement.

BDIX Tester should be designed to support a maintainable remote catalog-update mechanism.

### 8.1 Built-in Catalog

The application must include a built-in catalog fallback.

The initial catalog must remain usable without internet access.

A user must be able to open the server directory even if remote catalog services are unavailable.

### 8.2 Remote Catalog

Future updates may use a small, versioned JSON catalog served over HTTPS.

Do not invent a production backend endpoint.

Research and document suitable hosting options before implementation.

Possible hosting approaches may include:

- A controlled GitHub-hosted versioned JSON source.
- A dedicated HTTPS endpoint.
- Another maintainable static-content distribution service.

Evaluate availability, maintenance effort, security, caching, rate limits and long-term ownership.

### 8.3 Catalog Schema

Design a versioned catalog structure capable of representing:

- Schema version.
- Catalog version.
- Generated timestamp.
- Published timestamp.
- Expiration metadata, if used.
- Minimum compatible application version.
- Server identifier.
- Display name.
- URL.
- Protocol.
- Category.
